==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm}}, from {{der|en|fro|enviruner}}, {{m|fro|environner||to surround}}, from {{m|fro|environ||around}}, from {{m|fro|en||in}} + {{m|fro|viron||a turn}}, from {{m|fro|virer||to turn, veer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈvaɪ.ɹən/|/ɛnˈvaɪ.ɹən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪɹən|s=3}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-environ.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|especially in plural}} A [[surrounding]] [[area]]
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1811|author=[[s:Author:Jane Austen|Jane Austen]]|title=[[s:Sense and Sensibility|Sense and Sensibility]]|section=[[s:Sense and Sensibility/Chapter 19|Chapter 19]]|passage=His spirits, during the last two or three days, though still very unequal, were greatly improved—he grew more and more partial to the house and '''environs'''—never spoke of going away without a sigh [...]}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[encircle]], to [[surround#Verb|surround]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Titus Andronicus Q1|act=III|scene=i|page=51|passage=For now I ſtand as one vpon a rocke, / '''Inuirond''' with a wildernes of ſea, / VVho markes the waxing tide, grow waue by waue, / Expecting euer when ſome enuious ſurge, / VVill in his briniſh bowels ſwallow him.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=III|canto=V|stanza=39|passage=Dwelling in a pleasant glade, / With mountains round about '''environed'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-3|act=II|scene=i|passage='''Environed''' he was with many foes.}}
#* '''a. 1631''', {{w|John Donne}}, ''Elegy XII: His Parting from Her''
#*: '''Environ''' me with darkness whilst I write.
#* '''1673''', [[w:John Milton|John Milton]], “[[s:I did but prompt the age to quit their cloggs|I did but prompt the age to quit their cloggs]]”:
#*: I did but prompt the age to quit their cloggs
#*: By the known rules of antient libertie,
#*: When strait a barbarous noise '''environs''' me
#*: Of Owles and Cuckoes, Asses, Apes and Doggs.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1894|author=Henry Gough|author2=James Parker|title=A Glossary of Terms Used in Heraldry|page=231
|text=Azure, an annulet '''environing''' a barrulet, between two bars, and in chief &amp; cross patty fitchy {{...}} }}

